{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-c0f0e496d037056b5862","statement":"Note that if $(S,s,\\eta)$ is a trait, Lemma <<ref:LA reform>> says that $\\mF$ is locally acyclic with respect to $f$ if and only if $\\mF_s\\to \\Psi(\\mF_\\eta)$ is an isomorphism, or equivalently the vanishing cycles $\\Phi(\\mF)$ vanish.\nTherefore, for a higher dimensional base $S$, roughly speaking a sheaf $\\mF$ is ULA with respect to $f: X\\to S$ if there are no vanishing cycles along any direction on $S$. This can be made precise by introducing nearby cycles and vanishing cycles functors over higher dimensional base (cf. <<cite:Il3>>).","source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","statement_sha256":"539df7a8284604d0b6bdebbff2ce170b81ff7bd594fc54ada99459cb953bbe66","kind":"remark","label":"Remark 209","ref_key":"LA explanation","name":"","order":256,"deps":[{"ref":"LA reform","card_id":"ma-c-320c5b761d84d9689482","label":"Lemma 208","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":["Il3"],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"9aa0de800bec9f56ae36a0522194f91bc11ab1fe49bff0d4068568a9eb549a68","line":3563,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T16:49:20+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":539,"math_hints":29}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","title":"Guide for Lecturers in the Park City Mathematics Institute","abstract":"We introduce various affine Grassmannians, study their geometric properties, and give some applications. We also discuss the geometric Satake equivalence. These are the expanded lecture notes for a mini-course in 2015 PCMI summer school. References updated and more details added.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","macros":{"on":"\\operatorname","fraka":"{\\